    {
      "index": 19,
      "type": "text",
      "moduleId": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Below are some snippets of our logo building process. We knew we wanted an \"icon and text\" logo for flexibility — we could imagine someday these assets belonging on physical print reports, or a T-shirt, but also as a 32px favicon, or an email signature.",
          "links": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "There are lots of directions for climate tech branding: sun imagery for growth and power; grid imagery for reliability and strength; earth imagery for unification and humanity. I ended up picking an icon (top left option) that was closer to the pupil of an eye: always watchful, ready to act, and technologically vigilant so that we can stand at the foreground of climate policy.",
          "links": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The sundial-like partition of the circle nods toward our goal of implementing hourly Renewable Energy Certification: if there is no solar power at 11pm, a company should not be able to claim their energy consumption at 11pm comes from solar power.",
          "links": [
            {
              "href": "https://energytag.org/public-hearing-comment-on-the-amended-power-source-disclosure-regulations-docket-no-21-oir-01/",
              "text": "hourly Renewable Energy Certification"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "https://energytag.org/public-hearing-comment-on-the-amended-power-source-disclosure-regulations-docket-no-21-oir-01/",
          "text": "hourly Renewable Energy Certification"
        }
      ]
    },
